{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-35979","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58038","text":"TRAAVIIS — Environment Authoring Closure ("},{"id":"spn-58039","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs init"},{"id":"spn-58040","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-58041","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs pack"},{"id":"spn-58042","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-35980","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58043","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date"},{"id":"spn-58044","text":" 2026-07-24 · "},{"id":"spn-58045","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status"},{"id":"spn-58046","text":" shipped, 34 new laws green, full suite green "},{"id":"spn-58047","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope"},{"id":"spn-58048","text":" RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md §5, §5a, §6 — the first two items of the deferred surface that §7's build order unblocks once "},{"id":"spn-58049","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-58050","text":" exists."}]},{"id":"blk-35981","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58051","text":"1. What shipped"}]},{"id":"blk-35982","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58052","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-58053","text":" closed the beachhead: one agent, one frozen subject, one content-addressed receipt. But every bundle it could run had to be "},{"id":"spn-58054","marks":["italic"],"text":"hand-built"},{"id":"spn-58055","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-58056","marks":["code"],"text":"examples/eval-one/residency-forge/build_bundle.py"},{"id":"spn-58057","text":"). Authoring was the gap."}]},{"id":"blk-35983","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58058","text":"Two commands close it, and the split between them is the whole design:"}]},{"id":"blk-35984","kind":"code","language":"sh","text":"trvs init --list                                  # templates + their substrates\ntrvs init --template evidence-residency my-env    # seeds a subject + skeletons\ntrvs pack my-env my-env-pkg                       # closes it into a package\ntrvs eval-one my-env-pkg --agent … --platform linux-x86_64"},{"id":"blk-35985","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58059","text":"Verified end to end, from nothing to a scored episode:"}]},{"id":"blk-35986","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"init  →  8 files, identity: unresolved (init derives none)\npack  →  env-a38ec4c0…  snapshot snap-c66198ab…  task task-3b4b2599…\n         closure  ✓ verified before write\n         reopened ✓ re-derived from the written bytes\neval-one → status ✓ ok · validity valid · reward 1\n           citations pass · patch pass · tests pass · identity pass ·\n           finding_completeness pass"},{"id":"blk-35987","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58060","text":"The scaffolded residency subject recomputes to "},{"id":"spn-58061","marks":["bold"],"text":"exactly"},{"id":"spn-58062","text":" the frozen example's "},{"id":"spn-58063","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-c66198abf3ef6153d4bd6033fa40a0bd0028df3a7699ab645dc947710e51cba4"},{"id":"spn-58064","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-58065","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-25c4ce1276a7b70a473548354ae5d14f1c852ba087ffd09bc9b17b550c5c05a5"},{"id":"spn-58066","text":", and the "},{"id":"spn-58067","marks":["code"],"text":"golden-spinner"},{"id":"spn-58068","text":" template lowers to the frozen demo world "},{"id":"spn-58069","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-8ae91fe9cbc5fd086ce4356d…fe4a"},{"id":"spn-58070","text":". The seeds are the real artifacts, not lookalikes."}]},{"id":"blk-35988","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58071","text":"2. The load-bearing decision: "},{"id":"spn-58072","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-58073","text":" derives nothing"}]},{"id":"blk-35989","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58074","text":"§6 says "},{"id":"spn-58075","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-58076","text":" \"invents no identity.\" Taken literally that forbids the obvious implementation — scaffolding a "},{"id":"spn-58077","marks":["code"],"text":"task.json"},{"id":"spn-58078","text":" with a "},{"id":"spn-58079","marks":["code"],"text":"reward_id"},{"id":"spn-58080","text":" in it — because a scaffold cannot know the hash of bytes the author has not written yet, and a placeholder hash is a lie that later verifies."}]},{"id":"blk-35990","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58081","text":"So the scaffold emits "},{"id":"spn-58082","marks":["bold"],"text":"references"},{"id":"spn-58083","text":", and packing is the substitution:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-35992","spans":[{"id":"spn-58084","text":"scaffold ("},{"id":"spn-58085","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-58086","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-35993","spans":[{"id":"spn-58087","text":"package ("},{"id":"spn-58088","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-58089","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-35991","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-35994","spans":[{"id":"spn-58090","marks":["code"],"text":"task.reward_spec: \"reward.json\""}]},{"id":"blk-35995","spans":[{"id":"spn-58091","marks":["code"],"text":"task.reward_id: \"rew-…\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-35996","spans":[{"id":"spn-58092","marks":["code"],"text":"subject.snapshot_def: \"snapshot_def.json\""}]},{"id":"blk-35997","spans":[{"id":"spn-58093","marks":["code"],"text":"subject.snapshot_id: \"snap-…\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-35998","spans":[{"id":"spn-58094","marks":["code"],"text":"identity_policy…"},{"id":"spn-58095","text":" "},{"id":"spn-58096","marks":["italic"],"text":"(no `before_id`)"}]},{"id":"blk-35999","spans":[{"id":"spn-58097","marks":["code"],"text":"before_id: \"sem-…\""},{"id":"spn-58098","text":" (lowered now)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36000","spans":[{"id":"spn-58099","marks":["italic"],"text":"(no `env_id`)"}]},{"id":"blk-36001","spans":[{"id":"spn-58100","marks":["code"],"text":"env_id: \"env-…\""}]}]]},{"id":"blk-36002","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58101","text":"That is why "},{"id":"spn-58102","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-58103","text":" needs no engine and "},{"id":"spn-58104","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-58105","text":" does. It also makes L1 mechanically checkable: "},{"id":"spn-58106","marks":["code"],"text":"scaffold.identity_violations()"},{"id":"spn-58107","text":" scans every emitted document for an identity "},{"id":"spn-58108","marks":["italic"],"text":"key"},{"id":"spn-58109","text":" at any depth "},{"id":"spn-58110","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-58111","text":" every emitted byte for an id-shaped literal, so a future template cannot quietly bake one in — including in prose."}]},{"id":"blk-36003","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58112","text":"The literal half fails "},{"id":"spn-58113","marks":["bold"],"text":"closed"},{"id":"spn-58114","text":". It used to be a "},{"id":"spn-58115","marks":["code"],"text":"<prefix>-[0-9a-f]{8,}"},{"id":"spn-58116","text":" regex, which matches a well-formed digest and "},{"id":"spn-58117","marks":["italic"],"text":"nothing else"},{"id":"spn-58118","text":": a rung-prefixed token it could not parse — "},{"id":"spn-58119","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-abcdef12ZZZ"},{"id":"spn-58120","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58121","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-ABCDEF1234567890"},{"id":"spn-58122","text":", or the same id under a changed grammar ("},{"id":"spn-58123","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-jcs1-…"},{"id":"spn-58124","text":") — produced no match, and a guard that finds no id reports no violation, so a typo and a scheme change both read as \"clean\". "},{"id":"spn-58125","marks":["code"],"text":"scaffold.id_tokens"},{"id":"spn-58126","text":" now recognises the "},{"id":"spn-58127","marks":["bold"],"text":"rung prefix first"},{"id":"spn-58128","text":" (from the one "},{"id":"spn-58129","marks":["code"],"text":"ID_RUNGS"},{"id":"spn-58130","text":" list, which "},{"id":"spn-58131","marks":["code"],"text":"test_scaffold"},{"id":"spn-58132","text":"'s L1c pins against the ids "},{"id":"spn-58133","marks":["code"],"text":"identity.py"},{"id":"spn-58134","text":" actually mints) and then asks whether the remainder is a digest. Three verdicts: "},{"id":"spn-58135","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-58136","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58137","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"},{"id":"spn-58138","text":" (a known rung whose remainder does not parse) and "},{"id":"spn-58139","marks":["code"],"text":"unknown"},{"id":"spn-58140","text":" (a digest under a rung nobody should have minted). All three are violations. The elision form "},{"id":"spn-58141","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-58142","text":" is deliberately "},{"id":"spn-58143","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-58144","text":" a token — writing \"an id goes here\" asserts none."}]},{"id":"blk-36004","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58145","text":"What the guard does not report, and why that is written down"}]},{"id":"blk-36005","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58146","text":"The first version of this rewrite claimed the three verdicts \"leave no token that is both id-shaped and unreported\". That sentence was false in "},{"id":"spn-58147","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-58148","text":" directions, and each direction is a way a guard stops guarding:"}]},{"id":"blk-36006","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36008","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58149","text":"It was "},{"id":"spn-58150","marks":["bold"],"text":"narrower than the regex it replaced"},{"id":"spn-58151","text":". A lookbehind refused to begin"}]}],"id":"blk-36007","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-36009","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58152","text":"a token after "},{"id":"spn-58153","marks":["code"],"text":"-"},{"id":"spn-58154","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-58155","marks":["code"],"text":"."},{"id":"spn-58156","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-58157","marks":["code"],"text":"prev-episode-42d0bb07e5f83e9e"},{"id":"spn-58158","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-58159","marks":["code"],"text":"run.episode-42d0bb07e5f83e9e"},{"id":"spn-58160","text":" — which the old "},{"id":"spn-58161","marks":["code"],"text":"\\b"},{"id":"spn-58162","text":"-anchored regex reported — came back as "},{"id":"spn-58163","marks":["code"],"text":"[]"},{"id":"spn-58164","text":". A real, well-formed id, completely unreported. The lookbehind was standing in for something genuine ("},{"id":"spn-58165","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.finding- completeness-impl.v1"},{"id":"spn-58166","text":" is a declared verifier version present in every "},{"id":"spn-58167","marks":["code"],"text":"ComparisonV1"},{"id":"spn-58168","text":", and reading it as the "},{"id":"spn-58169","marks":["code"],"text":"finding"},{"id":"spn-58170","text":" rung failed "},{"id":"spn-58171","marks":["code"],"text":"test_compare"},{"id":"spn-58172","text":"'s C20), but it paid for that with coverage and no law recorded the trade."}]},{"id":"blk-36010","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36012","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58173","text":"It was "},{"id":"spn-58174","marks":["bold"],"text":"wider on prose"},{"id":"spn-58175","text":". Every hyphenated phrase whose first word happened"}]}],"id":"blk-36011","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-36013","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58176","text":"to be a rung name — "},{"id":"spn-58177","marks":["code"],"text":"env-vars"},{"id":"spn-58178","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58179","marks":["code"],"text":"task-oriented"},{"id":"spn-58180","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58181","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-apply"},{"id":"spn-58182","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58183","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-ver"},{"id":"spn-58184","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58185","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-path"},{"id":"spn-58186","text":" — was reported as a malformed id. A guard that cries wolf is switched off by the next person to trip it, which is fail-open by a slower route. Swept over this repository plus its build artifacts and sealed bundles (~56,000 documents), the rewrite produced "},{"id":"spn-58187","marks":["bold"],"text":"419"},{"id":"spn-58188","text":" non-"},{"id":"spn-58189","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-58190","text":" verdicts where the current guard produces "},{"id":"spn-58191","marks":["bold"],"text":"29"},{"id":"spn-58192","text":". The ~60 distinct tokens it dropped are all prose or identifiers — "},{"id":"spn-58193","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-bundle"},{"id":"spn-58194","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58195","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-fixture"},{"id":"spn-58196","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58197","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-ver"},{"id":"spn-58198","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58199","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-fail"},{"id":"spn-58200","text":" — including "},{"id":"spn-58201","marks":["bold"],"text":"`task-b`, which appears in real packed `env.json` and `TRAAVIIS_BUNDLE.json` documents"},{"id":"spn-58202","text":": the rewrite called a task "},{"id":"spn-58203","marks":["italic"],"text":"filename"},{"id":"spn-58204","text":" a malformed id. What survives as "},{"id":"spn-58205","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"},{"id":"spn-58206","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-58207","marks":["code"],"text":"*-PLACEHOLDER"},{"id":"spn-58208","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58209","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-abcdef12ZZZ"},{"id":"spn-58210","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58211","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-ABCDEF1234567890"},{"id":"spn-58212","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-58213","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-jcs1-…"},{"id":"spn-58214","text":" — every one an id-shaped token, and none of them prose."}]},{"id":"blk-36014","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58215","text":"The first defect is not visible as a count, and saying so is part of the record: committed text almost never writes an id inside a compound, which is exactly why nobody noticed it was no longer being read. It is demonstrated instead by planting — "},{"id":"spn-58216","marks":["code"],"text":"prev-episode-<64 hex>"},{"id":"spn-58217","text":" written into a real scaffolded template and into a real "},{"id":"spn-58218","marks":["code"],"text":"ComparisonV1"},{"id":"spn-58219","text":", where the legacy regex reports it, the rewrite reports nothing, and the current guard reports it again."}]},{"id":"blk-36015","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58220","text":"The discrimination that keeps both properties is the "},{"id":"spn-58221","marks":["bold"],"text":"remainder's shape"},{"id":"spn-58222","text":", with position gating only the "},{"id":"spn-58223","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"},{"id":"spn-58224","text":" verdict and never the "},{"id":"spn-58225","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-58226","text":" one:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-36017","spans":[{"id":"spn-58227","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-36018","spans":[{"id":"spn-58228","text":"reported"}]}],"id":"blk-36016","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-36019","spans":[{"id":"spn-58229","text":"a well-formed digest, anywhere — "},{"id":"spn-58230","marks":["code"],"text":"prev-episode-<hex>"},{"id":"spn-58231","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58232","marks":["code"],"text":"run.episode-<hex>"}]},{"id":"blk-36020","spans":[{"id":"spn-58233","marks":["bold"],"text":"yes"},{"id":"spn-58234","text":", as "},{"id":"spn-58235","marks":["code"],"text":"id"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36021","spans":[{"id":"spn-58236","text":"a rung + a remainder bearing a digit, an uppercase letter, or a run ≥ 16"}]},{"id":"blk-36022","spans":[{"id":"spn-58237","marks":["bold"],"text":"yes"},{"id":"spn-58238","text":", as "},{"id":"spn-58239","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36023","spans":[{"id":"spn-58240","text":"a rung + lowercase words of ordinary length — "},{"id":"spn-58241","marks":["code"],"text":"env-vars"},{"id":"spn-58242","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58243","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-nonsense"}]},{"id":"blk-36024","spans":[{"id":"spn-58244","text":"no"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36025","spans":[{"id":"spn-58245","text":"a rung "},{"id":"spn-58246","marks":["italic"],"text":"embedded"},{"id":"spn-58247","text":" in a compound name without a digest — "},{"id":"spn-58248","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.finding-completeness-impl.v1"},{"id":"spn-58249","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58250","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis-snap-01uu24ob"}]},{"id":"blk-36026","spans":[{"id":"spn-58251","text":"no"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-36027","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58252","text":"The third row is a "},{"id":"spn-58253","marks":["bold"],"text":"stated trade, not a discrimination"},{"id":"spn-58254","text":": "},{"id":"spn-58255","marks":["code"],"text":"nonsense"},{"id":"spn-58256","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-58257","marks":["code"],"text":"oriented"},{"id":"spn-58258","text":" are both eight lowercase letters with the same hex-letter density, and no lexical rule separates a typo'd id whose remainder happens to be word-shaped from an English phrase. What bounds the silence is that one edit in any direction — a digit, an uppercase letter, a longer run, an actual digest — puts the token back in scope. A mangled sha256 keeps its digits; a word has none. Both silences are pinned by "},{"id":"spn-58259","marks":["code"],"text":"test_scaffold"},{"id":"spn-58260","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-58261","marks":["bold"],"text":"L1g"},{"id":"spn-58262","text":", and the boundary by "},{"id":"spn-58263","marks":["bold"],"text":"L1e"},{"id":"spn-58264","text":", so widening either has to move a law rather than a comment."}]},{"id":"blk-36028","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58265","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-58266","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-58267","text":" follows §6's order literally"}]},{"id":"blk-36029","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"1. validate_subject             well-formed for the profile\n2. recompute_subject_identity   snap-… / sem-… FROM THE BYTES\n3. bind + close                 rew-… → task-… → env-…\n4. verify_closure               every reference resolves\n--- nothing has been written yet ---\n5. write                        temp tree → one os.replace\n6. reopen_package               re-derive every id from what landed on disk"},{"id":"blk-36030","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58268","text":"Step 6 is not ceremony. "},{"id":"spn-58269","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-58270","text":" deliberately does not trust its own in-memory computation: it reads the package back, re-derives "},{"id":"spn-58271","marks":["code"],"text":"env-"},{"id":"spn-58272","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-58273","marks":["code"],"text":"task-"},{"id":"spn-58274","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-58275","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-"},{"id":"spn-58276","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-58277","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-"},{"id":"spn-58278","text":" from the written bytes, "},{"id":"spn-58279","marks":["bold"],"text":"rebuilds the snapshot from the written subject tree"},{"id":"spn-58280","text":", and re-lowers the written world. If any of that disagrees, the package is removed and the command fails. Tampering with a packed task, or with one byte of a packed subject, is caught ("},{"id":"spn-58281","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_TASK_ID"},{"id":"spn-58282","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58283","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_SUBJECT_BYTES"},{"id":"spn-58284","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-36031","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58285","text":"Everything is fail-closed with a typed code: "},{"id":"spn-58286","marks":["code"],"text":"SOURCE_PREBOUND"},{"id":"spn-58287","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58288","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBJECT_DRIFT"},{"id":"spn-58289","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58290","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBJECT_KIND"},{"id":"spn-58291","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58292","marks":["code"],"text":"CLOSURE_VERIFIER"},{"id":"spn-58293","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58294","marks":["code"],"text":"CLOSURE_SUBJECT_BINDING"},{"id":"spn-58295","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58296","marks":["code"],"text":"SPLIT_UNRESOLVED"},{"id":"spn-58297","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58298","marks":["code"],"text":"DEST_NOT_EMPTY"},{"id":"spn-58299","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58300","marks":["code"],"text":"ENGINE_UNAVAILABLE"},{"id":"spn-58301","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58302","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_*"},{"id":"spn-58303","text":". A refused pack writes nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-36032","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58304","text":"4. The §5a admission interface is real"}]},{"id":"blk-36033","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58305","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/substrates.py"},{"id":"spn-58306","text":" implements "},{"id":"spn-58307","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_subject · verify_closure · recompute_subject_identity · reopen_package"},{"id":"spn-58308","text":" as a base class plus two profiles:"}]},{"id":"blk-36034","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36036","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58309","marks":["code"],"text":"trvm.world.v1"},{"id":"spn-58310","text":" — subject is WRL source; identity is "},{"id":"spn-58311","marks":["code"],"text":"engine.lower_source()"},{"id":"spn-58312","text":" →"}]}],"id":"blk-36035","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-36037","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58313","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-58314","text":"; reopen re-lowers the written world."}]},{"id":"blk-36038","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36040","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58315","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-58316","text":" — subject is a repository; identity is"}]}],"id":"blk-36039","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-36041","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58317","marks":["code"],"text":"snapshot.build_snapshot()"},{"id":"spn-58318","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-58319","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-58320","text":"; reopen rebuilds it from the written tree; closure additionally checks the verifier plan is "},{"id":"spn-58321","marks":["italic"],"text":"answerable by the reward it is bound to"},{"id":"spn-58322","text":" and that the test plan declares a runner profile."}]},{"id":"blk-36042","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58323","text":"The packer branches on profile in exactly two places (which subject bytes to copy, and the eval-bundle emission). A third substrate is a new profile object, not a new branch — which was the point of §5a."}]},{"id":"blk-36043","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58324","text":"5. Laws (34 new, all green)"}]},{"id":"blk-36044","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58325","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_scaffold.py"},{"id":"spn-58326","text":" — 16 laws: L1 invents no identity (incl. a planted-id detector test, so the check itself is proven to fire) · L2 deterministic (pure + on-disk) · L3 substrate-distinct · L4 declared frozen versions · L5 fail-closed + atomic (non-empty dest refused, mid-write failure leaves no partial tree and no temp dir) · L6 admissible input (snapshot definition matches the seeded tree exactly; both seeded worlds lower) · L7 portable (no absolute/host paths) · plus the CLI contract."}]},{"id":"blk-36045","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58327","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_pack.py"},{"id":"spn-58328","text":" — 18 laws: P1 every id recomputed, pre-bound ids refused · P2 content moves identity (subject bytes → "},{"id":"spn-58329","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-"},{"id":"spn-58330","text":"+"},{"id":"spn-58331","marks":["code"],"text":"env-"},{"id":"spn-58332","text":"; task instructions → "},{"id":"spn-58333","marks":["code"],"text":"task-"},{"id":"spn-58334","text":"+"},{"id":"spn-58335","marks":["code"],"text":"env-"},{"id":"spn-58336","text":") · "},{"id":"spn-58337","marks":["bold"],"text":"P3 presentation does NOT move `env-`"},{"id":"spn-58338","text":" (renaming + rewriting the description is byte-for-byte the same "},{"id":"spn-58339","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-58340","text":") · P4/P5 closure verified before write, nothing written on refusal, subject drift caught · P6 tampering fails reopen (task and subject) · P7 "},{"id":"spn-58341","marks":["code"],"text":"before_id"},{"id":"spn-58342","text":" is computed, and a declared one is refused · P8 determinism · P9 the TRVM profile lowers + reopens, and is a typed failure with no engine · P10 the packed environment actually runs to reward 1.0."}]},{"id":"blk-36046","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58343","text":"Regression: full suite green — identity 25, snapshot 10, reward 17, admission 16, paths 10, execfacts 8, vcontext 5, patchapply 10, verifiers 15, runner 10, evalone 14, substrate_verifiers 24, forge_adapter 6, cli_evalone 18, real_residency 9, episode_evidence 56."}]},{"id":"blk-36047","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58344","text":"6. Autonomous decisions — flagged for GPT-5.6"}]},{"id":"blk-36048","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36050","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58345","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scaffold-level references + `residency.snapshot-def.v1`."},{"id":"spn-58346","text":" §5 names a"}]}],"id":"blk-36049","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-36051","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58347","text":"\"snapshot definition\" as the scaffolded residency artifact; I gave it its own version string rather than emitting a "},{"id":"spn-58348","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.snapshot.v1"},{"id":"spn-58349","text":" with empty hashes. Confirm the name."}]},{"id":"blk-36052","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36054","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58350","marks":["bold"],"text":"`env-` identity allowlist excludes `name` and `description`."},{"id":"spn-58351","text":" §5 says"}]}],"id":"blk-36053","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-36055","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58352","text":"presentation-only edits move "},{"id":"spn-58353","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-58354","text":" only, so this is implemented as an explicit allowlist (like "},{"id":"spn-58355","marks":["code"],"text":"canonicalize_episode"},{"id":"spn-58356","text":") rather than by convention. Confirm "},{"id":"spn-58357","marks":["code"],"text":"name"},{"id":"spn-58358","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-58359","marks":["code"],"text":"description"},{"id":"spn-58360","text":" are presentation."}]},{"id":"blk-36056","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36058","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58361","marks":["bold"],"text":"`bundle-…` is not implemented."},{"id":"spn-58362","text":" "},{"id":"spn-58363","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-58364","text":" emits a package "},{"id":"spn-58365","marks":["italic"],"text":"directory"},{"id":"spn-58366","text":" and an"}]}],"id":"blk-36057","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-36059","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58367","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-58368","text":"; the outer content-addressed distributed package id from D3 is still open. This is the remaining half of §5 and I did not invent it."}]},{"id":"blk-36060","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36062","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58369","marks":["bold"],"text":"Single-task residency packages also emit `bundle.json`"},{"id":"spn-58370","text":" so "},{"id":"spn-58371","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-58372","text":" output is"}]}],"id":"blk-36061","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-36063","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58373","text":"directly runnable by "},{"id":"spn-58374","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-58375","text":". Multi-task packages do "},{"id":"spn-58376","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-58377","text":" get one (they would need a split-runner, i.e. "},{"id":"spn-58378","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-58379","text":") — deferred rather than emitted half-true."}]},{"id":"blk-36064","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36066","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58380","marks":["bold"],"text":"`pack` soft-loads the engine."},{"id":"spn-58381","text":" "},{"id":"spn-58382","marks":["code"],"text":"ENGINE_UNAVAILABLE"},{"id":"spn-58383","text":" is a typed admission"}]}],"id":"blk-36065","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-36067","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58384","text":"failure, so a residency pack that needs no lowering still works on a machine with no TRVM checkout."}]},{"id":"blk-36068","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36070","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58385","marks":["bold"],"text":"`RemoveObject`-style non-cascading discipline kept"},{"id":"spn-58386","text":": "},{"id":"spn-58387","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-58388","text":" never repairs a"}]}],"id":"blk-36069","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":6},{"id":"blk-36071","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58389","text":"scaffold. Subject drift is an error, not an auto-sync."}]},{"id":"blk-36072","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58390","text":"7. Not built (deferred, per ruling)"}]},{"id":"blk-36073","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58391","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-58392","text":" (splits), "},{"id":"spn-58393","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs serve --ors/--mcp"},{"id":"spn-58394","text":" (adapters over the Episode Kernel), "},{"id":"spn-58395","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-58396","text":", and the REPL. §7's order puts "},{"id":"spn-58397","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-58398","text":" next; "},{"id":"spn-58399","marks":["code"],"text":"serve"},{"id":"spn-58400","text":" needs the D5 process model, which is specified but unbuilt."}]},{"id":"blk-36074","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58401","text":"MIT licensed · TRAAVIIS Holdings · part of the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera6m4wqvpzvbmgbfwthklkzp2er4b7su26mkq3lbvjinbjg54jww3q","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}